MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two frame-time fixes:

1. ExitFunctionEC (Module.S) now translates the branch target through the
   iOS alias table before jumping to native EC code. PE images can't
   execute at their mapped address on iOS — the only runnable copy is in
   the dual-mapped JIT pool — so every x64→EC call was landing on the PE
   VA and eating a ~33us Mach exec-fault redirect. Measured ~40K faults
   per frame in Thumper's menu/gameplay (= the entire 1.4s frame time);
   after this, ~165/present. Menu+gameplay went 1.x → 15-20 FPS on
   iPhone 13 Pro. IosJitAlias.cpp storage is now extern "C"
   (IosAliasEntries/IosAliasCount) so the asm can reach it via adrp/lo12.

2. Dispatcher loop-top now probes the L1 lookup cache before the L2 page
   table (Dispatcher.cpp). L2 masks to VirtualMemSize (64GB) and Wine
   maps DLLs at ~0x7EExxxxxxxxx, so every DLL-code lookup aliased, failed
   the compare, and fell into the ~60us C++ CompileBlock path (~15K per
   menu frame). The warm L1 (full 64-bit compare) turns those into ~ns
   hits.

Also: CB_SUMMARY now logs L1Pointer/L1Mask/LookupCache-L1 for cache
diagnostics; per-block IR logging silenced (Core.cpp).

